🔧 Normal Development Build (on your host)
Nothing changes. You can continue developing and testing on your local machine just as before:

bash
cd build
cmake .. -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug -G Ninja
ninja
./NohBoard
This will use your system’s libraries and is perfect for quick iterations.

📦 Building a New AppImage (after code changes)
Whenever you modify the code and want to create an updated AppImage, simply run the same script:

bash
sudo ./build-appimage.sh
This will:

Re‑run the Docker build, copying your latest source code into the container.

Compile the application inside the Ubuntu 20.04 environment.

Bundle all dependencies (Qt, X11, Wayland, etc.) into a new AppImage.

Place the final NohBoard-*.AppImage into the dist/ folder.

The process is completely automated and reproducible—you don’t need to clean anything manually.



x86_64-w64-mingw32.static-cmake .. -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
make -j4
